ould each be  the same distance away from the middle  once you have something like this just  make sure it's nice and flat and then we  can flip it over now you'll see we have  a center point here I'm just going to  mark and we're going to take each of the  edges here and fold it down to the  center point so let's take this one here  I'm just going to round it off a little  bit like this and fold this edge down to  that Center mark when I fold it down to  the center mark you'll see this other  corner will come up all right but we're  not going to fold it on the outside here  we're going to be pressing on the inside  of this little pocket area so just take  the edge pull it down to the middle it's  easier to do this on a table once the  edge is lined up like that then just  make a crease right here just press it  like that and just crease to the left  side then we could just push our finger  in this little pocket area here like  that just give it a press it will go  right up to this corner here you don't  want to crease on the outside here so  once we crease like that then we can  unfold it turn it and we're going to do  the same with this edge fold it directly  down to the center point press it down  in the middle like that press right here  and crease all the way to the left  give it a nice sharp crease and just  press right in this little pocket area  unfold it turn it do the same with these  two just like the other two fold the  edge straight down to the middle crease  to the left and press in the pocket  finally with the last one  same thing edge straight down crease it  all the way across and press in the  pocket so now if you unfold everything  you'll have something that looks just  like this we're going to do the same  thing that we did on the other side  where we closed them all to create the  windmill except we're going to be doing  it in a counterclockwise direction now  so I'm just going to pinch this little  corner here and I'm going to press  here like 